{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe weather turned foul on Sunday, and I, in my usual haste, overlooked the early start at the Hofoper. I arrived at seven, far too late for the opening chorus in praise of Franz. A minor tragedy, but I made the best of it. We heard the first act of *Zelmira*. Dardanelli was decent, but Lablache was a bore. Donzelli, however, sang a recitative that was quite exquisite—pure, clear, and without affectation. I paid six florins for a good seat, which I consider fair for the evening’s entertainment.\n\nThe food at the theatre was mediocre, as usual, so I dined on simple soup and bread. I think of you and the boys, and the quiet of our home in Berlin. The noise here is tiresome.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219024,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":186,"prompt_tokens":1112,"total_tokens":1298,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-rrESPuKPNdqHjCHF9LnK2zjTUV4JXyjE","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1112,"prompt_ms":1135.727,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0213372302158275,"prompt_per_second":979.1085357660776,"predicted_n":186,"predicted_ms":4377.2,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.660540540540538,"predicted_per_second":42.26446129946085}}